From 473840125edaacc5b2c6e49f6987843d2d062481 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 22:22:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 26/42] transports+configstore: tenant-scoped customers CRUD
 under /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/customers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mirror of patch 0025 for the customer entity. Same delegate-then-
verify pattern with tenant_id re-pinning to defend against migration
via PUT. Customers are also tagging metadata (not request-path state)
so the runtime evictor is not wired here — mutations show up on
subsequent admin reads + on any VK whose customer_id pointer the
operator updates.

Routes:
  POST   /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/customers
  GET    /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/customers
  GET    /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/customers/{customer_id}
  PUT    /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/customers/{customer_id}
  DELETE /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/customers/{customer_id}

configstore additions: CreateCustomerForTenant, GetCustomersByTenant,
GetCustomerByIDForTenant, UpdateCustomerForTenant,
DeleteCustomerForTenant + MockConfigStore stubs + 2 configstore tests
(full CRUD across two tenants + malicious payload defense).
Transport: TenantCustomersHandler with 7 handler tests.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
